<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Tobacco up 1.56 pct on results.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Tobacco up 1.56 pct on results.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ceylon Tobacco Co Ltd rose 1.56 percent or 50 cents to 32.50 on Wednesday on improved 1996 profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The price movement is purely on good growth figures which were just released,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>The company earlier said its net profit for the year to December 31, 1996 rose 21.6 percent to 575.22 million rupees compared to 472.95 million rupees in the same period of the previous financial year.</p>
<p>Ceylon Tobacco, Sri Lanka's main cigarette maker, is a subsidiary of Britain's BAT Industries Plc.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
